  "title": "Long-lived Agent Session Orchestration",
  "description": "# Long-lived agent session orchestration\n\nA lifecycle and systems diagram showing how a shared control plane places durable AI-agent sessions, runs the turn loop on runner hosts, streams output while persisting an identical event history, checkpoints immutable content-addressed state, and resumes or recovers work on any eligible host.\n\nRead left-to-right across the top for admission and execution, then downward through durable state, recovery, session trees and quotas, and lifecycle operations. Solid arrows carry primary control or data; dashed arrows show recovery, propagation, and operational feedback.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
